Subject: [PATCH] U0 update

USB U0: measured baseline + docs/plans/USB_PLAN.md.

Baseline measured 2026-10-09 on AuraLite-Emulator@fbbc8bd with
AuraLite-OS@0ed0d29 (kernel.elf + initrd.tar built from that tree) and
the sample firmware. What the machine presents today: a behavioural
EHCI block (PCI 0:3.0, scratch BAR0 window, zeroed capability
registers, doorbell on every register write, one CBW special case --
READ(10)/READ(12) plus a fabricated CSW with tag=0/residue=0/status=OK,
SETUP ignored). What the guest expects (measured): msc.c validates
dCSWTag/residue/status and enumerates with INQUIRY, READ CAPACITY(10),
TEST UNIT READY, REQUEST SENSE; ehci.c runs the halt handshake and the
PORTSC/companion path; uhci.c needs an I/O BAR4 + frame list. The U0
kernel-lane receipts capture the honest state: HCI version 0.00,
0 ports, controller did not halt, 0 device(s) enumerated, no UHCI
controller. Eleven measured defects drive U1-U5 (BOT/CSW, SCSI opcodes,
USBCMD-only doorbell + caps/PORTSC/control, UHCI parity with the QEMU
run_qemu_usb_msc.sh/test_usbfs.sh contract, end-to-end receipts).

ROADMAP: USB row -> IN PROGRESS (U0 done); stale CORE/CHIPSET ledger
rows corrected to match their plan files (C0-C11, H0-H7 done).
